{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"moral status of ai moral status of ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md","fileName":"Moral Status of AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Moral Status of AI","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Machine Moral Status]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Machine Moral Agency","Machine Moral Patiency","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"moral status of ai moral status of ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md","fileName":"Moral Status of AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Moral Status of AI","heading":"Moral Status of AI","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The moral status of AI concerns where an artificial system belongs within moral relationships. It combines two distinct questions: whether the system can be a [[Machine Moral Agency|moral agent]] whose actions can be evaluated, and whether it can be a [[Machine Moral Patiency|moral patient]] toward which others have duties.\n\nThese questions need not have the same answer. A machine might reliably follow moral constraints without deserving praise or blame, or people might have reasons not to abuse a robot even if it lacks experience. Moral status can be based on internal capacities, socially ascribed relationships, or the effects that treatment of machines has on humans.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Machine Moral Agency","Machine Moral Patiency","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"moral status of ai moral status of ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Moral Status of AI.md","fileName":"Moral Status of AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Moral Status of AI","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Machine Moral Agency","Machine Moral Patiency","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}